<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<TcPlcObject Version="1.1.0.1" ProductVersion="3.1.4024.12">
  <POU Name="FB_SolenoidPair" Id="{23ddf2e7-415d-4237-9e6d-fcc92e4bc96b}" SpecialFunc="None">
    <Declaration><![CDATA[(*
    FB_SolenoidPair - driver for one mutually exclusive solenoid valve pair.

    PURPOSE
        Drives one pair of solenoid valves so that only one of the two is ever
        commanded open. The pair is selected by a single EPICS switch: valve 01
        is open while i_xEpics is FALSE and valve 02 is open while i_xEpics is
        TRUE. The block owns that mutual exclusion - while the debug bypass is
        off it writes the two outputs as complements every cycle, never both.

    USAGE
        Instantiated once per solenoid pair and called unconditionally every
        PLC cycle. The block has no VAR_INPUT / VAR_OUTPUT: the switch, the
        debug bypass and both outputs are AT %I* / AT %Q* links wired by the
        caller's TcLinkTo pragma, e.g. in EXAMPLE_DEPLOYMENT:

            {attribute 'TcLinkTo' := '
                .q_xDO1 := TIIB[Solenoid Pair A Digital IO (EP2338-0001)]^Channel 9^Output;
                .q_xDO2 := TIIB[Solenoid Pair A Digital IO (EP2338-0001)]^Channel 10^Output;'}
            fbSolenoidPairA : FB_SolenoidPair;

        The caller must also link i_xEpics (the Switch PV) and i_xDebug (the
        Debug PV). Both valve outputs carry io: io, so EPICS reads the state
        back, and while the debug bypass is TRUE EPICS also writes it.

    OBJECTIVES
        - Keep the pair mutually exclusive: while i_xDebug is FALSE, q_xDO1 is
          written as NOT i_xEpics and q_xDO2 as i_xEpics, so the two valves can
          never be commanded open at the same time.
        - Leave both outputs untouched while i_xDebug is TRUE, so an operator
          can open each valve independently from EPICS for commissioning and
          leak checking.
        - Publish what each output does through pytmc field metadata - both
          valve PVs carry ZNAM "CLOSE" / ONAM "OPEN".
        - Hold no state of its own: the outputs are a straight function of the
          two inputs, so dropping the debug bypass restores the A/B selection
          on the very next cycle.

    PRECONDITIONS
        - i_xEpics and i_xDebug must be linked by the caller. An unlinked %I*
          input reads FALSE, which selects valve 01.
        - The Debug PV is a maintenance bypass of the mutual exclusion only.
          While it is TRUE nothing in this block prevents both valves from being
          commanded open, so it must be off for normal operation.
        - The outputs are levels, not timed commands: they are rewritten every
          cycle and the valves are passive solenoids on the digital outputs, so
          the block has no completion wait, timeout or fault output of its own.

    HISTORY
        2026-11-27 / Scirix Agent
            Added this header and the q_xDO1 / q_xDO2 declaration comments;
            documentation only, no behaviour change (audit finding #908,
            convention conv_321640e095c0).
        Earlier author/date history was not recorded in this file. The block
        came in with the original LCLS sample-delivery code (2023-05-19) and
        has since only gained PV metadata - 2025-06-25, ZNAM/ONAM field
        attributes on the two valve PVs (J. Zamudio).
*)
FUNCTION_BLOCK FB_SolenoidPair
VAR_INPUT
END_VAR
VAR_OUTPUT
END_VAR
VAR_IN_OUT
END_VAR
VAR
    {attribute 'pytmc' := '
        pv: Valve:01:Open
        io: io
        field: ZNAM "CLOSE"
        field: ONAM "OPEN"
     '}
    (* Valve 01 solenoid output (PV Valve:01:Open). TRUE = output ON, valve
       01 commanded OPEN (ONAM); FALSE = output OFF, valve 01 commanded
       CLOSED (ZNAM). Written as NOT i_xEpics while the debug bypass
       i_xDebug is FALSE, and left to EPICS while i_xDebug is TRUE. *)
    q_xDO1 AT %Q*	:	BOOL;
    {attribute 'pytmc' := '
        pv: Valve:02:Open
        io: io
        field: ZNAM "CLOSE"
        field: ONAM "OPEN"
     '}
    (* Valve 02 solenoid output (PV Valve:02:Open). TRUE = output ON, valve
       02 commanded OPEN (ONAM); FALSE = output OFF, valve 02 commanded
       CLOSED (ZNAM). Written as i_xEpics while the debug bypass i_xDebug
       is FALSE, and left to EPICS while i_xDebug is TRUE. *)
    q_xDO2 AT %Q*	:	BOOL;

    {attribute 'pytmc' := '
        pv: Switch
        io: o
     '}
    i_xEpics AT %I* : BOOL; // open A when False, open B when True

    {attribute 'pytmc' := '
        pv: Debug
        io: o
     '}
    i_xDebug AT %I* : BOOL; // if True, do not set valves according to i_xEpics
END_VAR
]]></Declaration>
    <Implementation>
      <ST><![CDATA[(* If debug, set independently. Else, only open one valve according to i_xEpics *)
IF NOT i_xDebug THEN
    q_xDO1 := NOT i_xEpics;
    q_xDO2 := i_xEpics;
END_IF]]></ST>
    </Implementation>
  </POU>
</TcPlcObject>